sections.text:
Python scripts run on an embedded real CPython interpreter — the full standard library is available, and exports bundle it with your game. A script file contains exactly one horizon.Behavior subclass; typed class attributes become editor-exposed properties: spinner.py import horizon

class Spinner(horizon.Behavior):
    speed = 90.0  # exposed in the Details panel

    def on_start(self):
        self.angle = 0.0

    def on_update(self, dt):
        self.angle += self.speed * dt
        horizon.setRotation(self.entity_id, 0, self.angle, 0) The API mirrors Lua exactly — the same function names, with vectors returned as tuples and raycast returning a dict (or None on miss).

